# The storyboard's stills and their receipts are committed (frames/, frames/light/, web/, game/, player/, cut/, the
# contact sheets and index.json). What renders and captures write beside them stays out of git; git add -f takes one
# in on purpose.
#
# PNG sequences a film is encoded from: scripts/capture-story.mjs writes <out>/frames/<i>.png, by default under
# player/film-<cut>/. The top-level frames/ holds the stills and is not matched.
*/**/frames/
# Films: master.mp4 is about 150 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB file limit. Each film's .json receipt carries its size and
# SHA-256.
*.mp4
*.webm
*.mov
# Stills from capture-story.mjs --times (t-<seconds>.png).
player/t-*.png
